  "summary": "Six preprints apply multi-omic, long-read and graph methods to resolve immune states, including interferon-alpha and CD40 programs in Sjögren's disease.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is computational resolution of immune heterogeneity from high-dimensional data rather than a single interferon finding. The most direct interferon item uses mGEDO to define interferon-alpha and CD40 signatures in Sjögren's disease, with distinct transcripto-methylomic profiles suggesting complementary immune programs for patient stratification. Related work resolves bystander versus tumor-specific T cells with a multimodal graph neural network integrating transcriptomes and TCR sequences, and identifies a CTLA4-high naive CD4 T cell subpopulation in aging through subsampling-based analysis. Others derive cell-type-resolved epigenetic clocks from long-read methylation data, link gene-dependency network structure in CAR T infusion products to treatment failure risk, and show that CHIP driver mutations have heterogeneous effects. Evidence is preprint-only.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-28"
}
